# platform.geek.display

The GEEK boards' ST7789 panel: 240 by 135 in landscape, RGB565, on SPI1 with
the backlight on GP25, clocked at 62.5 MHz as the family's other ST7789 boards
are, which the Pico's SPI rounds down to what its divider holds. The 135-row
panel sits inside the controller's 240 by 320 frame memory at column 40 and
row 53 once memory access 0x70 turns it on its side. It owns the wiring and
the panel's porch, power, and gamma settings, and registers the controller as
mm.display. rp2040_geek and rp2350_geek both bind it.
